WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.620
WHAT IF

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.750
TIME

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.770
Suppose you were able to stop time for three minutes.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.000
What would you do?

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.320
Moritani?

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:48.260
Huh?

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.530
Come on, were you not listening?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.740
Oh, s-sorry, I was spacing out.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.960
You see, I've read short stories by that author before.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.280
R-Really?

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.880
I was thinking of reading one of their novels next.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.130
You got any recommendations?

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.820
Uh, I... Um...

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.640
Um...

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.430
It was...

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:38.020
It was as a fleeting dream...

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:41.770
Huh? Why aren't you frozen?

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.310
What is eternity like?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.310
<i>I stopped time...</i>

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.580
<i>Did you do this?</i>

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.520
<i>And then I got found out...</i>

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.980
H-How did you know—

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.270
And wait, Murakami, how come you can move?

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.930
Can you stop time for as long as you want?

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.940
J-Just three minutes.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.100
Three minutes, huh?

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.370
That's short.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.900
You went as far as to stop time
just to get a peek at my underwear?

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:27.960
Huh?

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.450
You're a real creep, aren't you?

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.760
N-N-No, that's not what I—

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.110
Wonder how people would react if I told them.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:42.100
How the normally timid, inconspicuous Moritani...

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:51.860
...is actually a creep who goes around looking at other girls' underwear.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.910
No, wait! I'll do anything you want!

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.820
<i>I had no idea...</i>

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:57.860
Anything?

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.150
<i>...Murakami was like that.</i>

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.860
You'll really do anything?

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.220
<i>She's a bit mean.</i>

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.370
<i>But... Even so...</i>

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:22.130
<i>She's so pretty that I get nervous around her.</i>

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:25.980
What should I have you do?

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.980
I'll think of something for tomorrow.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.020
<i>She'll "think of something"?</i>

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.690
<i>I wonder what she'll make me do...</i>

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:46.830
Good morning, Moritani!

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.650
Ah! I'm sorry!

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:49.150
Huh?

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:51.300
Uh... G-Good morning.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.600
Something the matter?

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.750
No, it's nothing.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:59.360
By the way, Moritani,
you haven't joined a club yet, have you?

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.110
Huh? No...

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.640
How about the ping pong club?

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.910
We're running low on members, see.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:08.140
I mean... I'm already a second year...

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.520
No matter!

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.270
We're pretty easy-going,
so we don't mind people joining later.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.070
Why don't you stop by after school?

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.540
<i>Come on...</i>

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:18.940
<i>Why does she have to come talk to me every single day?</i>

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:20.700
So if—

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.570
Oh?

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.290
You stop time over something like this?

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.620
And now you're off to look up girls' skirts, are you?

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:40.130
What? I-I wouldn't do that!

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.580
But you looked up mine yesterday.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.790
I-I've never done that with anyone else.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:48.710
Th-That was my first time...

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:49.760
Really?

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.560
Yes, really.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.750
Well, that aside,

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.110
time really has stopped, huh?

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.550
It wasn't a dream after all.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.240
<i>I wish it </i>was<i> just a dream!</i>

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.230
Am I the only one who can move?

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:05.130
I think so...

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.640
I wonder why it's just me.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.040
I-I have no idea.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:13.290
<i>If I knew that, I'd make sure
Murakami was frozen too!</i>

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.700
So you stopped time,

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.110
but I, and only I, can still move.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:23.430
That's got to be because you're interested in me, no?

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:23.970
Huh?

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:27.700
You wanted to share this time with me,
and no one else.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.430
That must be it.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.790
In other words...

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.640
<i>I can't...</i>

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.210
You've got a crush on me.

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:41.400
<i>I can't keep up with Murakami.</i>

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.650
By the way...

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.030
You free this Sunday?

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.900
<i>When was the last time I spent
my time off with someone?</i>

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.280
Hey, you alone?
I'll take you somewhere fun.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:58.340
Moritani!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.110
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:05.580
Oh, no, I...

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:09.050
Let's get this date started.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:09.680
What?

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:12.600
<i>D-Date?!</i>

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.820
This is so good!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.330
Here, try some.

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.820
Hurry up! It's melting!

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.410
Come on, here!

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.500
Like it?

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.790
Are you sure you wanted to come here?

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.270
I'm fine with wherever you want to go.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:43.540
Y-Yeah.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:46.760
I-I want to go where you want to go.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.400
Really?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.420
No need to worry about me.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.230
Look at that girl! She's so pretty!

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:51.970
I know, right?

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.380
Wonder if she's a model or something.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.500
I wouldn't be surprised.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:01.790
<i>I want to stop time and run away.</i>

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:07.910
Hey, look! This would be perfect on you!

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:17.780
<i>But...</i>

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:21.200
I think I'll buy you a pair of these.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.210
Wha—

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.510
<i>She's not like other people.</i>

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:26.680
They're the same ones I'm wearing.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:27.840
Bet you want them.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.970
I mean, you were staring at them real hard.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:34.400
No! It's not the panties I'm interested in!

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.740
Not the panties, but?

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:40.210
<i>Being with Murakami...</i>

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:45.080
Oh yeah, it's me wearing these
that you're interested in.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.390
There you go again...

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.990
<i>is so much fun.</i>

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.300
<i>Fun?</i>

00:09:54.730 --> 00:10:00.540
<i>Do I really deserve to have fun spending time with others?</i>

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.060
Hm?

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:14.890
Hey, what do you think of this?

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:15.890
Huh?

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.790
<i>It's Tamaki from our class.</i>

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:21.230
<i>Along with a girl from another class.</i>

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:23.690
Th-They seem to get along well.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:25.220
Think they're dating?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.950
I wonder when they got together.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.220
Wish he'd just told me.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:33.220
<i>What? Does she mean...</i>

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:37.450
Murakami, were you and Tamaki...

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.620
We were going out.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.830
Though I guess I'm not his girlfriend anymore.

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:48.200
<i>What? So he got together with another girl in secret?</i>

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.380
<i>No, that can't...</i>

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.620
Let's go.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.220
What?

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.550
<i>What?!</i>

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.850
Are you sure about this?

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:00.500
I mean, if you two were going out,

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:01.960
that's awful of Tamaki!

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:02.820
You should tell him—

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:05.100
Not like I actually loved him or anything.

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.620
He just asked me to go out with him, so I did.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:11.700
B-But then, what about your feelings?

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:13.630
They don't matter.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.410
<i>Murakami...</i>

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:24.370
<i>Why do you talk as if you've given up on everything?</i>

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:28.410
<i>Of course your feelings matter.</i>

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.360
Moritani?

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:49.900
Time has...

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.160
Murakami! No one will know if you do it now!

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:58.450
Hurry!

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:11.630
<i>Maybe Murakami is right.</i>

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:16.010
<i>The reason I'm still able to move when you stop time...</i>

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.630
<i>...is because I want to spend time together with Murakami.</i>

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.480
<i>So, in other words...</i>

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:25.810
<i>You've got a crush on me.</i>

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:44.040
<i>We spent the following few days stopping time</i>

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:49.080
<i>and going around spying on our classmates' little secrets.</i>

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.490
<i>Murakami knows a lot about the other students.</i>

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:57.010
<i>Possibly even a bit </i>too<i> much.</i>

00:12:57.520 --> 00:13:00.630
Hey, are the three minutes up soon?

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:01.550
Yeah.

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:04.390
This is like our own secret time.

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:06.230
Makes me kind of excited.

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:09.020
Yeah, same here.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.190
See?

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:12.360
Huh? I, uh...

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.740
<i>Th-They're soft...</i>

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:18.060
Too bad you can't stop time for longer.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:26.830
Nice shot! Go!

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:31.370
Haruka! Mind joining our team?

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:32.840
Sure!

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:34.100
What? No fair!

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:36.300
Murakami, join ours instead!

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.260
No way, you've already got three basketball club members.

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:42.720
Haruka's worth ten people! That's not fair!

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.770
<i>Everybody loves Murakami.</i>

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.420
Nice shot, Haruka.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:01.870
Thanks.

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:05.120
All right! One more rou—

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:10.710
Moritani.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.380
<i>Huh? What?</i>

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:16.250
What's wrong? Why did you stop time?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.260
Uh... Well...

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:21.220
<i>I did it without thinking.</i>

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:23.420
You were running around so much,

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.970
so I figured maybe you needed a break.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:29.390
I see. Thanks.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.400
<i>What the heck am I doing?</i>

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:35.870
Oh, I get it!

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.900
See? That's how you solve it in no time.

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:40.900
You're a lifesaver, thank you!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:41.990
The hero we need!

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:44.340
Always saving our butts.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:45.940
You're such a good teacher.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.240
Sorry we're so dumb.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.680
Thanks a lot.

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.090
Moritani.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.680
S-Sorry.

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:03.340
I did it by mistake.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:05.510
I see...

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:09.830
<i>Murakami is loved by everyone, not just me.</i>

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:14.230
W-Well, since time is already stopped and all,
could you help me with a problem?

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.460
I mean, sure. Which one?

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:19.030
Um, well, it's...

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.810
<i>What the heck am I doing?</i>

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.580
<i>I can stop time all I want,</i>

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:33.280
<i>but I can't keep Murakami to myself.</i>

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.760
Good morning, Haruka!

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:42.960
Morning.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.830
Hey, did you hear about Tamaki?

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:46.300
Huh?

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:46.780
What?

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:47.390
What about him?

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:52.230
Oh yeah, you mean how he put a pair of panties on his head while on a date?

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:54.530
Seriously? What a freak.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:55.940
Did you know about that, Haruka?

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:57.640
Oh, yeah, I heard it somewhere.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:00.870
Man, who does that?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.120
What's up, Moritani?

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:09.480
<i>It wasn't on purpose.</i>

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:10.900
<i>It wasn't on purpose, although...</i>

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.080
Th-That's strange...

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:15.280
My power's been acting up lately...

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.250
<i>Or rather, my emotions have been acting up...</i>

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:18.960
Why are you lying?

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.580
Are you jealous?

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.180
You were feeling lonely, so—

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:28.060
No, you're wrong! I'm not jealous!

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:31.350
Really, I swear, it's just by accident.

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:32.270
If you say so.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:37.840
Moritani.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:38.520
Yes?

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.800
If you <i>are</i> doing it on purpose,

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:42.980
you should probably stop.

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:54.340
<i>"You should probably stop"...</i>

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.550
<i>What Murakami said...</i>

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:21.460
<i>...keeps turning over in my mind.</i>

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:24.390
<i>Murakami is probably fed up with me.</i>

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:28.990
<i>And that thought...</i>

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:30.870
<i>...scares me.</i>

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:39.090
<i>Days went by without anything being resolved.</i>

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.630
May I go to the nurse's office? My stomach hurts.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.860
What am I doing?

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:50.510
This is just stupid.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:55.380
There's someone sleeping, so keep it down.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.270
Okay.

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:07.450
You haven't been stopping time lately.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:08.260
Why not?

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:13.450
Because you told me I should stop.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:17.660
I don't want to get on your bad side.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:19.710
You're blaming it on me?

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.570
No!

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:24.670
You have to come to terms with what you truly want to do.

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:27.430
What I truly want to do?

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:28.070
Yup.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:31.410
I couldn't tell you that.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:32.400
Why not?

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.640
If I did, you'd get upset.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.730
You'd make me upset...

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:47.480
At that rate, you'll never be able to share your true feelings with anyone.

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:57.450
Isn't it almost time for class?

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.700
Once you're feeling better, you should head back to—

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:19.880
You're able to stop time for about three minutes, right?

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:21.390
Yeah.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:25.500
So if I were to kiss you right here and now...

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:29.520
Time would start ticking again,
and the nurse would see us.

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:33.330
I don't mind, you know.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:38.790
I'd be fine with someone seeing us kiss.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:03.010
Once you're feeling better, head back to the classroom.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:03.930
Okay!

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.370
<i>Why don't you go out with me?</i>

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:32.840
<i>Go out?</i>

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:38.180
<i>If you go out with me,
I'll stop talking to other people.</i>

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:40.050
<i>In return...</i>

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.570
<i>In return?</i>

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:47.250
<i>In return...</i>

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.610
<i>In return?</i>

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.790
<i>...will you let me do something?</i>

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:10.040
Moritani, remind me,
where'd you go for junior high?

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.690
Huh? Me?

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.570
Um... Well...

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.590
You went to a different school from us, right?

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:20.180
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.530
Minami Junior High.

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:26.120
Oh yeah? There's not a lot of
people from Minami here.

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:27.930
R-Really?

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:31.700
Oh right, I finally got that lip balm everyone's been going on about.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:32.380
Yeah?

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:33.550
The strawberry one.

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:37.750
Hey, Haruka. Could you help us with the homework for fifth period?

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:38.880
Not again!

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.030
You guys are too dependent on her.

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:42.280
Sorry.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.350
Don't worry.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:44.740
Hold on, I'll get my notebook.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:45.910
You're the best!

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:47.810
In that case, I guess I'll join you.

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:49.040
You too?!

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:56.300
<i>Who knew talking to people without stopping time</i>

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:58.760
<i>would be this draining?</i>

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:01.380
<i>Doesn't Murakami ever get tired of dealing with people?</i>

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:05.250
Oh, come on! These false eyelashes come off too easy!

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:07.290
You just touch your face too much.

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:09.770
Gotta say though, that Moritani girl?

00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:12.560
I wish she'd actually, like, reply to questions.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:13.730
I know, right?

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:17.330
Whenever you ask her something,
she just goes quiet.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.320
What's Haruka thinking?

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:20.880
Yeah...

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:24.220
But Murakami's always sucking up to people, isn't she?

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:25.890
Oh, I know what you mean.

00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:27.660
Constantly trying to please others.

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:29.660
Always making eyes at guys too.

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.600
Did you hear about her and Yamaguchi,
the homeroom teacher?

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:35.230
What? How she lets him touch her?

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:36.440
Is that for real?

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:37.960
So that's why she gets special treatment.

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:40.480
Well, I wouldn't be surprised.

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:43.270
I mean, sure, it would be fun to be popular,

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:46.060
but Yamaguchi having his eyes on you? Screw that!

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:48.490
You reap what you sow, I'd say.

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:50.050
Oh, don't tell her I said that.

00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:52.280
Yeah, I know.

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:54.230
<i>I remember now.</i>

00:22:55.630 --> 00:22:59.430
<i>This is why I can't get along with others.</i>

00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:03.260
<i>All these superficial relationships.</i>

00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:07.310
<i>I hated having to be with others so much,</i>

00:23:08.710 --> 00:23:10.240
<i>that I lived my life running away.</i>

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:14.490
<i>But what about people who can't flee,</i>

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.830
<i>like Murakami?</i>

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:21.170
<i>Doesn't she have it even worse?</i>

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.550
Okay, you can start.

00:23:49.930 --> 00:23:51.830
Can you take my picture?

00:23:51.830 --> 00:23:52.830
Picture?

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:55.460
Pay close attention to me.

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:59.420
Sure, I will.

00:24:01.900 --> 00:24:03.610
I wouldn't take my eyes off you.

00:24:25.620 --> 00:24:26.360
Come here.

00:24:34.010 --> 00:24:36.040
Go ahead and satisfy your desire.

00:24:56.670 --> 00:24:58.350
No one's watching.

00:24:59.210 --> 00:25:00.430
Now's your chance.

00:25:08.110 --> 00:25:11.570
<i>When I touch her, I can feel her heart racing.</i>

00:25:20.060 --> 00:25:22.870
<i>The beloved model student Murakami</i>

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:26.670
<i>wants to be a bad girl.</i>

00:25:37.170 --> 00:25:40.480
<i>Murakami... Murakami...</i>

00:25:40.840 --> 00:25:43.940
<i>Murakami... Murakami...</i>

00:25:44.340 --> 00:25:47.440
<i>You have to put your clothes back on!
Time will start ticking again!</i>

00:25:50.910 --> 00:25:54.870
<i>Murakami almost looked disappointed.</i>

00:25:55.390 --> 00:25:59.870
<i>As if she didn't mind being found out.</i>

00:26:00.320 --> 00:26:02.880
<i>Will she do the same thing tomorrow too?</i>

00:26:03.400 --> 00:26:06.540
<i>Murakami... Murakami...</i>

00:26:11.960 --> 00:26:13.550
Moritani!

00:26:13.550 --> 00:26:14.740
Murakami?!

00:26:15.410 --> 00:26:17.290
Um... I believe my name's Kobayashi.

00:26:17.290 --> 00:26:18.980
S-Sorry...

00:26:18.980 --> 00:26:20.020
Don't sweat it.

00:26:20.680 --> 00:26:23.980
You <i>have</i> been spending
a lot of time with Murakami lately.

00:26:24.310 --> 00:26:26.650
Are you joining the same club as her, or what?

00:26:26.650 --> 00:26:28.460
Huh? No, not really.

00:26:28.460 --> 00:26:32.280
Really?! Then have you given some thought to what I said about the ping pong club?

00:26:32.280 --> 00:26:32.950
Ping pong?

00:26:34.970 --> 00:26:38.890
<i>Oh right, she mentioned something about that before.</i>

00:26:38.890 --> 00:26:41.470
I-I'm not really good at sports.

00:26:41.470 --> 00:26:42.830
No worries!

00:26:42.830 --> 00:26:44.320
See, it's also called table tennis,

00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:46.750
and it's way easier to get into than other sports.

00:26:46.750 --> 00:26:48.260
And just between you and me,

00:26:48.260 --> 00:26:51.550
the school isn't really expecting anything from us.

00:26:51.550 --> 00:26:54.400
<i>Maybe I'll stop time and run away again...</i>

00:26:55.510 --> 00:26:57.550
You can start with practice swings!

00:26:57.550 --> 00:27:01.020
<i>No, I have to save my time for Murakami.</i>

00:27:02.720 --> 00:27:05.560
You're actually listening to what I have to say today, huh?

00:27:05.570 --> 00:27:06.620
Huh?

00:27:06.620 --> 00:27:09.940
Whenever I talk to you,
you always disappear somewhere.

00:27:09.940 --> 00:27:12.780
I was worried I was bothering you or something.

00:27:12.780 --> 00:27:14.910
S-Sorry, that wasn't my intention...

00:27:16.210 --> 00:27:17.370
That's a relief.

00:27:19.250 --> 00:27:21.290
Let's eat!

00:27:24.770 --> 00:27:26.630
Moritani, you've got strawberry milk!

00:27:27.010 --> 00:27:28.340
Mind if I have some?

00:27:28.340 --> 00:27:29.340
Oh, sure.

00:27:32.350 --> 00:27:34.220
<i>That's an indirect k—</i>

00:27:34.220 --> 00:27:35.710
Thanks!

00:27:35.710 --> 00:27:38.530
Your food looks great. Wanna trade with me?

00:27:38.530 --> 00:27:40.270
Sure, here you go.

00:27:40.990 --> 00:27:44.310
<i>H-How can they be so intimate?</i>

00:27:44.310 --> 00:27:47.020
Yukari, your octopus sausages are so cute!

00:27:47.020 --> 00:27:48.790
Did you make the same for your siblings?

00:27:48.790 --> 00:27:51.240
Yup! They really love these.

00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:53.930
I wish I could be your little sister!

00:27:53.930 --> 00:27:56.910
Making enough for you would kill me.

00:27:59.580 --> 00:28:02.960
<i>Is this what girls are like with each other?</i>

00:28:03.900 --> 00:28:06.290
So what's she like, really?

00:28:06.290 --> 00:28:08.960
Huh? Sorry, what was that?

00:28:08.960 --> 00:28:10.630
I mean Murakami.

00:28:10.940 --> 00:28:13.660
She's kind of scary to talk to, you know?

00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:15.340
Yeah, now that you mention it.

00:28:15.620 --> 00:28:18.100
I don't think I've ever had a real conversation with her.

00:28:18.100 --> 00:28:20.410
You seem pretty close to her, Moritani.

00:28:20.410 --> 00:28:22.220
How'd you end up friends?

00:28:22.220 --> 00:28:25.310
Uh... I'm not really sure...

00:28:25.310 --> 00:28:26.790
<i>I can't tell them</i>

00:28:26.790 --> 00:28:30.150
<i>it's because I stopped time and looked up her skirt.</i>

00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:43.040
<i>She seemed lonely...</i>

00:28:43.460 --> 00:28:44.760
<i>I must be imagining it.</i>

00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:56.140
Haruka!

00:29:01.060 --> 00:29:02.760
Sorry about tha—

00:29:08.270 --> 00:29:10.010
Moritani?

00:29:10.670 --> 00:29:12.270
Why did you stop time?

00:29:19.980 --> 00:29:22.250
Suddenly feel like talking to me?

00:29:22.250 --> 00:29:23.330
Or...

00:29:26.270 --> 00:29:27.500
...is all.

00:29:28.510 --> 00:29:29.170
Huh?

00:29:30.010 --> 00:29:32.180
You looked sad, is all.

00:29:33.490 --> 00:29:36.420
Sorry, that's just what it seemed like to me.

00:29:36.420 --> 00:29:39.710
Every once in a while, you'll gaze off
into the distance, you know?

00:29:39.710 --> 00:29:43.500
I was thinking maybe that's a sign that you're tired or something.

00:29:43.500 --> 00:29:45.520
You've seemed really busy lately.

00:29:45.940 --> 00:29:51.140
Oh yeah, I never sent you the photos from when we stopped time the other day.

00:29:51.140 --> 00:29:52.020
I don't want them.

00:29:59.650 --> 00:30:01.730
I'd like you to keep them.

00:30:02.640 --> 00:30:05.690
To remind yourself that it really happened.

00:30:09.980 --> 00:30:11.780
Haruka, when did you get over there?

00:30:11.780 --> 00:30:12.380
Huh?

00:30:12.880 --> 00:30:15.870
You just disappeared from your desk with a poof.

00:30:15.870 --> 00:30:17.730
That's silly.

00:30:17.730 --> 00:30:18.640
Let's head home.

00:30:18.640 --> 00:30:19.840
Y-Yeah.

00:30:20.780 --> 00:30:26.620
"To remind yourself that it really happened."

00:30:31.620 --> 00:30:34.150
Moritani? Moritani!

00:30:36.070 --> 00:30:37.400
Moritani!

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:41.590
Are you not feeling well?
Wanna stop by the nurse's office?

00:30:41.590 --> 00:30:43.760
I-I'm fine.

00:30:44.860 --> 00:30:47.420
How about some fresh air, then?

00:30:47.420 --> 00:30:47.990
Come on, let's go.

00:30:47.990 --> 00:30:48.370
Huh?

00:30:48.370 --> 00:30:49.960
O-Okay.

00:30:57.240 --> 00:30:58.900
I feel so much better.

00:30:58.900 --> 00:31:01.720
Maybe you were running low on oxygen.

00:31:01.720 --> 00:31:03.960
What did you put down for your career plans?

00:31:03.960 --> 00:31:05.520
Nothing yet.

00:31:05.520 --> 00:31:06.940
What about you?

00:31:07.430 --> 00:31:08.680
What?! A comic artist?!

00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:10.280
Shh! Keep it down!

00:31:10.280 --> 00:31:11.650
S-Sorry.

00:31:11.650 --> 00:31:13.720
Don't tell anyone, okay?

00:31:13.720 --> 00:31:17.070
Everyone else is probably planning on going to university,

00:31:17.070 --> 00:31:20.820
but I figured I might as well give it a try
before I start looking for a job.

00:31:20.820 --> 00:31:22.980
That's incredible, Kobayashi.

00:31:22.980 --> 00:31:26.180
Nah, I'm just naive.

00:31:26.180 --> 00:31:28.300
I'm writing a ping pong manga right now.

00:31:28.300 --> 00:31:31.200
I'm using my club experience to make it as realistic as I can.

00:31:31.940 --> 00:31:33.040
Huh...

00:31:33.940 --> 00:31:36.000
<i>Career plans...</i>

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:37.380
<i>I...</i>

00:31:38.670 --> 00:31:41.880
<i>...don't even know what will happen today.</i>

00:31:42.550 --> 00:31:45.260
Isn't that someone's career plans form on the floor?

00:31:45.260 --> 00:31:46.350
It's Kobayashi's.

00:31:46.350 --> 00:31:47.430
A comic artist?

00:31:47.430 --> 00:31:48.810
Seriously? Lemme see.

00:31:48.810 --> 00:31:51.090
No way, is that really what she's planning on doing?

00:31:51.090 --> 00:31:52.940
Sounds good to me. Make a hit and she'll be rich.

00:31:52.940 --> 00:31:55.730
Nothing about university.
Giving up on studies, huh?

00:31:55.730 --> 00:31:57.310
Got her head in the clouds.

00:31:58.040 --> 00:31:59.650
Moritani!

00:32:10.550 --> 00:32:12.440
Murakami, wait!

00:32:14.040 --> 00:32:17.750
Remember what I promised when we agreed to go out?

00:32:17.750 --> 00:32:22.180
I said I wouldn't be alone with anyone other than you.

00:32:22.180 --> 00:32:23.660
I've been keeping that promise.

00:32:23.660 --> 00:32:25.720
Whenever I'm talking to someone,

00:32:25.720 --> 00:32:29.610
I make sure to bring someone else into the conversation so we're not alone.

00:32:29.610 --> 00:32:34.100
But I guess I was the only one who cared.

00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:37.350
No, you're wrong, Murakami! Look!

00:32:37.350 --> 00:32:41.360
I'm always thinking about you.

00:32:41.360 --> 00:32:42.990
Just take these panties.

00:32:43.420 --> 00:32:47.780
I bought these online because
I wanted to wear a matching pair.

00:32:48.540 --> 00:32:49.780
No kidding.

00:32:50.990 --> 00:32:52.700
We match.

00:33:00.250 --> 00:33:02.400
<i>She really is crazy.</i>

00:33:03.570 --> 00:33:08.210
<i>But seeing Murakami smile like that,</i>

00:33:08.210 --> 00:33:12.640
<i>I was so happy that I didn't even care anymore.</i>

00:33:17.140 --> 00:33:19.060
<i>Three minutes.</i>

00:33:19.060 --> 00:33:22.150
<i>That's how long my and Murakami's world lasts.</i>

00:33:23.180 --> 00:33:27.520
<i>If only it could last longer.</i>

00:33:28.640 --> 00:33:33.300
<i>Forever, without any limits.</i>

00:33:37.740 --> 00:33:40.960
Our three minutes are almost up.

00:33:41.520 --> 00:33:45.260
Time is about to start ticking again.

00:33:45.260 --> 00:33:47.340
Don't worry.

00:33:52.440 --> 00:33:54.850
Look, everything's still frozen in time, isn't it?

00:33:58.540 --> 00:33:59.520
You're right.

00:34:00.100 --> 00:34:02.220
While time is stopped,

00:34:02.220 --> 00:34:04.320
there's also nothing to move time forward.

00:34:04.950 --> 00:34:07.530
There never was any time limit to begin with.

00:34:08.020 --> 00:34:11.530
Oh yeah, now that you mention it, you're right.

00:34:11.530 --> 00:34:13.190
That makes sense.

00:34:13.190 --> 00:34:17.250
Does that mean time is stopped forever?

00:34:17.250 --> 00:34:18.380
That's right.

00:34:18.890 --> 00:34:20.000
Look.

00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:23.140
Waves, stars, sand, and people.

00:34:23.140 --> 00:34:24.500
They're all frozen in time.

00:34:24.850 --> 00:34:27.820
And no clock is awake to count to three minutes.

00:34:27.820 --> 00:34:29.410
They're stopped for eternity.

00:34:30.300 --> 00:34:34.150
What is eternity like?

00:34:34.670 --> 00:34:36.310
Does the thought make you lonely?

00:34:36.310 --> 00:34:39.390
No, not as long as I have you!

00:34:41.520 --> 00:34:43.250
<i>But in reality,</i>

00:34:44.330 --> 00:34:48.360
<i>my power to stop time was growing weaker,</i>

00:34:49.790 --> 00:34:54.420
<i>and little by little, things began to fall apart.</i>

00:34:58.290 --> 00:34:59.810
She flashed her panties in the hallway?

00:34:59.810 --> 00:35:00.520
For real?

00:35:00.520 --> 00:35:02.360
Yeah, it's true. You saw it too, didn't you?

00:35:02.360 --> 00:35:03.970
Yeah, that was definitely Murakami.

00:35:03.970 --> 00:35:04.760
Haruka did?

00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:05.790
Apparently, yeah.

00:35:05.790 --> 00:35:07.930
Out of nowhere, with guys in the hallway.

00:35:07.930 --> 00:35:10.140
Seriously? Is she a flasher, or what?

00:35:10.140 --> 00:35:12.000
Pretty people can get away with anything.

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:14.670
She's kinda been weirding me out for a while,

00:35:14.670 --> 00:35:16.390
but this is too much.

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:19.460
And they say she's seeing Yamaguchi,
the homeroom teacher.

00:35:19.460 --> 00:35:20.350
Gross.

00:35:21.510 --> 00:35:24.360
<i>I don't know what to do.</i>

00:35:24.900 --> 00:35:26.240
On your mark.

00:35:29.700 --> 00:35:31.530
Thank you so much for yesterday.

00:35:31.530 --> 00:35:32.370
Huh?

00:35:32.370 --> 00:35:34.990
For finding my career plans form.

00:35:35.550 --> 00:35:38.450
I know becoming a comic artist is pretty unlikely,

00:35:38.450 --> 00:35:41.110
but it's been my dream ever since I was a kid.

00:35:42.370 --> 00:35:44.100
Mind if I ask something weird?

00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:44.900
Huh?

00:35:44.900 --> 00:35:47.300
So this is just a hypothetical...

00:35:47.300 --> 00:35:49.170
What is it? Just tell me!

00:35:50.060 --> 00:35:56.410
Say I had someone important to me,
and I thought I had the power to protect them,

00:35:56.410 --> 00:35:59.180
but then I became unable to use that power...

00:35:59.180 --> 00:36:03.420
A prince paying the medical fees for his frail lover

00:36:03.420 --> 00:36:04.600
goes bankrupt!

00:36:04.600 --> 00:36:06.530
Now what does he do?!

00:36:06.530 --> 00:36:07.660
Something like that?

00:36:07.660 --> 00:36:11.570
Huh? Y-Yeah, something to that effect.

00:36:11.570 --> 00:36:13.680
Nothing he can do in that case.

00:36:13.680 --> 00:36:16.660
The prince will just have to come clean to his lover.

00:36:17.300 --> 00:36:19.710
Huh? Was I too blunt there?

00:36:19.710 --> 00:36:21.500
No, it's just...

00:36:21.500 --> 00:36:26.590
What if that lover didn't care about anything but the money?

00:36:26.590 --> 00:36:29.330
Seriously? What a lowlife!
He should break up with her, pronto!

00:36:29.330 --> 00:36:31.460
Gold diggers are the absolute worst!

00:36:31.460 --> 00:36:34.010
Oh, but she supports him in some ways.

00:36:34.010 --> 00:36:34.970
Really?

00:36:34.970 --> 00:36:35.970
Maybe I'm imagining it...

00:36:35.970 --> 00:36:37.030
Which is it?!

00:36:37.030 --> 00:36:38.220
Um...

00:36:38.710 --> 00:36:41.460
The prince has fun when he's with his lover,

00:36:41.460 --> 00:36:43.460
and when she smiles, he's happy.

00:36:43.460 --> 00:36:46.310
So he still wants to be together with her.

00:36:46.640 --> 00:36:47.470
Right...

00:36:48.050 --> 00:36:50.920
So you're saying they both need each other?

00:36:50.920 --> 00:36:53.170
Isn't that what you call mutual love?

00:36:53.170 --> 00:36:54.810
R-Really?

00:36:54.810 --> 00:36:59.280
I bet she wants the prince to take it easier on himself and just talk to her.

00:36:59.820 --> 00:37:02.450
You wouldn't be talking about Murakami, would you?

00:37:02.450 --> 00:37:05.660
What? N-No, it's just a hypothetical!

00:37:05.660 --> 00:37:07.000
Yeah, I know.

00:37:07.800 --> 00:37:12.160
But I'm really glad that you
decided to ask me for advice.

00:37:12.160 --> 00:37:13.300
I never expected that.

00:37:15.060 --> 00:37:20.510
<i>And I never thought I'd be able to
talk to someone this casually.</i>

00:37:21.070 --> 00:37:24.020
<i>It must be thanks to spending time with Murakami.</i>

00:37:36.120 --> 00:37:39.410
There's something I need to tell you.

00:37:39.410 --> 00:37:40.530
I'm not interested.

00:37:41.250 --> 00:37:42.490
Wait!

00:37:43.240 --> 00:37:44.450
Murakami!

00:37:45.750 --> 00:37:49.920
I might lose my power to stop time!

00:37:49.920 --> 00:37:50.610
What?

00:37:56.090 --> 00:37:58.220
I can't stop time as easily as before.

00:37:58.220 --> 00:38:01.050
And the length of time is decreasing.

00:38:01.400 --> 00:38:04.700
So we won't be able to go wild like before, then.

00:38:05.590 --> 00:38:06.390
I'm sorry.

00:38:07.450 --> 00:38:10.160
You're still wearing your indoor shoes, you know.

00:38:10.160 --> 00:38:13.770
That's just because you ran off without warning!

00:38:14.270 --> 00:38:16.540
While you're still able to stop time,

00:38:17.650 --> 00:38:19.790
let's leave behind proof that we were here.

00:38:22.340 --> 00:38:23.410
Together.

00:38:28.210 --> 00:38:31.170
Aikawa's copying this part wrong!

00:38:31.170 --> 00:38:32.500
I'll fix it for her.

00:38:32.500 --> 00:38:34.530
W-Won't she find out?

00:38:34.530 --> 00:38:35.590
You think?

00:38:36.070 --> 00:38:38.040
Aikawa isn't the type to worry about details.

00:38:38.040 --> 00:38:39.750
I give her a 50% chance of noticing.

00:38:39.750 --> 00:38:44.400
I'll also write that she needs to be careful sleeping up front or she'll be caught.

00:38:44.400 --> 00:38:46.190
Wait, what are you—

00:38:46.190 --> 00:38:47.060
Too late.

00:38:47.060 --> 00:38:48.890
<i>During the days that followed,</i>

00:38:48.890 --> 00:38:51.340
<i>Murakami didn't do anything particularly outrageous.</i>

00:38:51.340 --> 00:38:52.770
Hey, who did this?!

00:38:52.770 --> 00:38:53.650
Huh? What's up?

00:38:53.650 --> 00:38:55.630
Someone's scribbled in my notebook.

00:38:55.630 --> 00:38:58.990
"If you use your birthday as your password, your boyfriend will open the lock."

00:38:58.990 --> 00:39:00.140
The heck's this?

00:39:00.140 --> 00:39:03.410
<i>I don't understand what she's trying to do.</i>

00:39:03.780 --> 00:39:08.340
<i>She'll undress in the classroom,
and leave behind notes for people to find.</i>

00:39:08.910 --> 00:39:11.250
That's right. Well done memorizing that.

00:39:11.250 --> 00:39:13.250
Now, on to the next task...

00:39:13.670 --> 00:39:15.430
See? He touched her shoulder.

00:39:15.430 --> 00:39:16.860
Doesn't that bother Murakami?

00:39:16.860 --> 00:39:19.130
A panty flasher like her wouldn't care.

00:39:19.130 --> 00:39:20.880
And she was kind of provocative to begin with.

00:39:20.880 --> 00:39:24.260
<i>Stop. I don't want to hear. I don't want to know.</i>

00:39:25.620 --> 00:39:27.230
I'm telling you, I don't know.

00:39:27.230 --> 00:39:28.680
No use hiding it, Tamaki.

00:39:29.110 --> 00:39:30.870
You used to date Murakami, right?

00:39:30.870 --> 00:39:32.160
Well, thing is,

00:39:32.160 --> 00:39:35.360
even when we were dating,
it didn't really feel like she cared about me.

00:39:35.820 --> 00:39:37.170
What about you, Moritani?

00:39:37.170 --> 00:39:38.650
How do you feel about me?

00:39:38.650 --> 00:39:41.320
I'll suddenly kiss you, show you my underwear,

00:39:41.320 --> 00:39:44.430
tell you to go out with me,
take my clothes off in the classroom...

00:39:44.940 --> 00:39:48.080
I'm sure you were thinking the same thing.

00:39:50.630 --> 00:39:51.690
Who would do this?

00:39:52.580 --> 00:39:56.710
I've tried to go along with people's wishes as best I can.

00:39:56.710 --> 00:39:57.790
"Show me your homework."

00:39:57.790 --> 00:39:59.190
"Explain this part."

00:39:59.190 --> 00:40:00.410
"Help me carry this."

00:40:00.410 --> 00:40:01.800
"Go out with me."

00:40:01.800 --> 00:40:03.880
"Something came up, can we reschedule?"

00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:07.340
I went along with all of it, and this is what I get.

00:40:07.340 --> 00:40:10.730
Whenever I asked you to stop time,

00:40:10.730 --> 00:40:13.840
you never asked why or what I wanted to do.

00:40:15.650 --> 00:40:16.650
I can tell.

00:40:17.320 --> 00:40:21.170
No one has any interest in knowing the true me.

00:40:22.030 --> 00:40:24.470
<i>That's right, I don't want to know.</i>

00:40:24.470 --> 00:40:26.870
<i>I don't want to know what she's really like.</i>

00:40:26.870 --> 00:40:29.140
<i>She's a bit mean, but she's actually kind.</i>

00:40:29.140 --> 00:40:31.430
<i>Just when I think she's kind, she becomes distant.</i>

00:40:31.430 --> 00:40:34.210
<i>And when I feel she's distant, next she...</i>

00:40:34.210 --> 00:40:36.490
<i>I don't want to know. But...</i>

00:40:36.490 --> 00:40:39.530
<i>Then I can't say I truly love Murakami.</i>

00:40:40.920 --> 00:40:43.340
<i>I want to understand Murakami.</i>

00:40:43.620 --> 00:40:47.930
Murakami! Can I visit your place sometime?

00:41:55.500 --> 00:41:57.120
Did you find it all right?

00:41:57.120 --> 00:41:59.620
Y-Yeah, no problem.

00:42:05.710 --> 00:42:07.670
P-Pardon the intrusion...

00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:10.410
You can take it easy.

00:42:10.410 --> 00:42:12.490
It's just the two of us until dark.

00:42:14.330 --> 00:42:16.690
You okay with Darjeeling tea?

00:42:16.690 --> 00:42:19.520
S-Sure. Thanks.

00:42:21.860 --> 00:42:25.510
Don't go snooping around the room while I'm gone.

00:42:29.610 --> 00:42:33.580
<i>When was the last time
I was in someone else's room?</i>

00:42:33.860 --> 00:42:37.120
<i>Murakami's room smells good.</i>

00:42:41.540 --> 00:42:43.400
You didn't touch anywhere funny, did you?

00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:44.970
No, I didn't.

00:42:44.970 --> 00:42:46.380
Really?

00:42:46.380 --> 00:42:47.350
Not even the bed?

00:42:47.350 --> 00:42:49.420
D-Did not!

00:42:52.780 --> 00:42:58.850
A-Anyway, the reason I came over is because I wanted a chance to talk to you properly.

00:42:58.850 --> 00:43:03.860
Otherwise we only really talk while time is stopped.

00:43:03.860 --> 00:43:08.070
I wanted to get to know you a bit better.

00:43:08.070 --> 00:43:09.020
Moritani.

00:43:09.020 --> 00:43:09.440
Huh?

00:43:09.440 --> 00:43:10.950
Come over here.

00:43:10.950 --> 00:43:11.670
Come on.

00:43:27.440 --> 00:43:29.550
Let's do what you want to do.

00:43:31.790 --> 00:43:32.880
No need to hold back.

00:43:35.330 --> 00:43:36.850
I don't like this.

00:43:37.340 --> 00:43:41.890
I can't imagine that this is what you want to do.

00:43:41.890 --> 00:43:44.390
Why do you do this, Murakami?

00:43:44.820 --> 00:43:46.470
That's a strange question.

00:43:56.830 --> 00:43:59.700
It's because this is what you want to do.

00:44:00.100 --> 00:44:01.280
What I want to?

00:44:01.280 --> 00:44:02.660
<i>What is she saying?</i>

00:44:02.660 --> 00:44:03.670
Am I wrong?

00:44:03.670 --> 00:44:05.500
<i>Does she mean...</i>

00:44:05.790 --> 00:44:07.920
It's what you want to do.

00:44:07.920 --> 00:44:09.680
Do you...

00:44:09.680 --> 00:44:12.630
<i>...only care about what others want?</i>

00:44:20.190 --> 00:44:21.120
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:44:22.310 --> 00:44:23.820
<i>I don't want to ask.</i>

00:44:24.340 --> 00:44:25.110
<i>But...</i>

00:44:27.190 --> 00:44:31.820
Murakami, why did you decide to go out with me?

00:44:32.280 --> 00:44:34.700
Could it be that...

00:44:39.970 --> 00:44:43.750
You thought I wanted you to go out with me,

00:44:43.750 --> 00:44:45.370
and that's why you did it?

00:45:00.500 --> 00:45:01.370
Give me a sec.

00:45:01.370 --> 00:45:02.960
My mom's back.

00:45:02.960 --> 00:45:04.230
She forgot something.

00:45:06.400 --> 00:45:09.650
Don't go searching anywhere while I'm gone.

00:45:10.120 --> 00:45:11.380
Especially not under the bed.

00:45:17.720 --> 00:45:19.080
<i>Don't go searching anywhere.</i>

00:45:28.840 --> 00:45:31.300
<i>She likes this.</i>

00:45:31.300 --> 00:45:33.260
<i>He likes that.</i>

00:45:34.280 --> 00:45:36.600
<i>That girl likes this.</i>

00:45:36.600 --> 00:45:38.720
<i>This boy likes that.</i>

00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:43.960
You'll be okay for dinner, then?

00:45:43.960 --> 00:45:45.610
Yeah, no worries.

00:45:45.610 --> 00:45:47.600
You make sure to eat too.

00:45:47.600 --> 00:45:48.600
Yes, I know.

00:45:58.790 --> 00:46:01.740
The names of every student and teacher.

00:46:01.740 --> 00:46:03.240
On the backs are birthdays,

00:46:03.240 --> 00:46:04.240
blood types,

00:46:04.570 --> 00:46:06.120
likes and dislikes,

00:46:06.450 --> 00:46:07.460
what makes them happy...

00:46:08.020 --> 00:46:11.870
You memorize all of these,
and act according to them?

00:46:13.830 --> 00:46:14.840
That's right.

00:46:15.350 --> 00:46:16.830
Did you see yours?

00:46:19.980 --> 00:46:21.340
Misuzu Moritani.

00:46:21.960 --> 00:46:24.500
"The reason she is always reading books alone

00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:27.040
is just that she is bad at talking to others."

00:46:27.040 --> 00:46:29.730
"She will easily grow fond of anyone who talks to her nicely."

00:46:29.730 --> 00:46:30.270
No, I—

00:46:30.270 --> 00:46:33.120
"She is actually very interested in others."

00:46:33.120 --> 00:46:34.860
"She just can't make the first move."

00:46:34.860 --> 00:46:38.050
"As long as someone is nice to her,
it doesn't matter who it is."

00:46:38.540 --> 00:46:41.220
"She wants to be the only one who understands that person."

00:46:41.780 --> 00:46:46.620
"She just needs an exciting ingredient like a shared secret."

00:46:47.630 --> 00:46:50.040
"If it is a girl, all the better."

00:46:51.070 --> 00:46:52.290
"It doesn't matter who."

00:46:52.290 --> 00:46:54.250
Stop it! That's not me!

00:46:54.690 --> 00:46:56.960
That's how all the people around me were.

00:46:56.960 --> 00:47:01.690
Friends are just tools high up in the social hierarchy

00:47:01.690 --> 00:47:04.850
that you use as accessories
to make yourself look stronger.

00:47:05.280 --> 00:47:06.350
Am I wrong?

00:47:07.900 --> 00:47:10.140
What everyone is looking for

00:47:10.140 --> 00:47:12.350
is someone kind, who they can rely on,

00:47:12.350 --> 00:47:14.560
who will help them without complaining,

00:47:14.560 --> 00:47:16.540
who won't say what they don't want to hear,

00:47:16.540 --> 00:47:18.310
and who will do anything she's asked.

00:47:18.310 --> 00:47:20.110
That's the Haruka Murakami they want.

00:47:21.300 --> 00:47:24.900
But what about your own feelings?

00:47:24.900 --> 00:47:28.440
You also have things you want to do, don't you?

00:47:28.440 --> 00:47:29.500
Let's have a look.

00:47:31.990 --> 00:47:33.770
Haruka Murakami.

00:47:33.770 --> 00:47:35.980
Wants to be liked by everyone.

00:47:36.920 --> 00:47:39.840
Tries to please everyone, disliked by no one.

00:47:40.410 --> 00:47:41.720
And you see,

00:47:42.130 --> 00:47:43.180
what happens then...

00:47:44.680 --> 00:47:46.220
...is that she's...

00:47:48.600 --> 00:47:50.680
...left with nothing.

00:48:19.810 --> 00:48:23.050
<i>If you just pretend you didn't see anything today,</i>

00:48:23.560 --> 00:48:27.470
<i>we can go back to being
"two girls secretly in love" tomorrow.</i>

00:48:28.030 --> 00:48:32.930
<i>Murakami can't fall in love with anyone or anything,</i>

00:48:32.930 --> 00:48:35.690
<i>and even during the three minutes that time is stopped,</i>

00:48:36.310 --> 00:48:38.280
<i>she has no idea what she wants to do.</i>

00:48:40.940 --> 00:48:44.240
<i>Is she really happy like that?</i>

00:48:44.240 --> 00:48:45.450
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:48:53.630 --> 00:48:59.630
<i>It's not something an outsider like me could hope to understand.</i>

00:48:59.630 --> 00:49:04.130
<i>It's impossible for anyone to truly understand someone else.</i>

00:49:05.210 --> 00:49:05.840
<i>So...</i>

00:49:06.450 --> 00:49:08.850
So you'll just have to live with that?

00:49:09.230 --> 00:49:10.350
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:49:11.940 --> 00:49:16.210
<i>But right now, our hands are firmly entwined.</i>

00:49:17.730 --> 00:49:18.770
<i>So...</i>

00:49:23.690 --> 00:49:25.740
Huh? What are they doing?

00:49:26.770 --> 00:49:27.820
Moritani?

00:49:28.390 --> 00:49:30.040
You knew time was about to...

00:49:31.330 --> 00:49:33.950
You can't run away today, Murakami.

00:49:35.460 --> 00:49:38.980
I, Misuzu Moritani, as well as Haruka Murakami

00:49:38.980 --> 00:49:43.340
have been stopping time to do
all kinds of crazy things together!

00:49:44.260 --> 00:49:46.680
We scribbled in people's notebooks,

00:49:46.680 --> 00:49:49.050
put panties on Tamaki's head after he cheated,

00:49:49.430 --> 00:49:51.510
took off our clothes in the classroom...

00:49:51.510 --> 00:49:53.490
What are you saying, Moritani?

00:49:53.490 --> 00:49:56.500
If you tell them that, then we can't...

00:49:57.090 --> 00:49:59.770
"We can't", what?

00:49:59.770 --> 00:50:01.980
Complete your sentence, Murakami!

00:50:08.920 --> 00:50:10.200
Murakami!

00:50:15.450 --> 00:50:18.080
Wait! Tell me, Murakami!

00:50:18.080 --> 00:50:22.460
You told me that you try to please everyone so that they'll like you.

00:50:23.160 --> 00:50:29.360
That means you wouldn't want anyone to know what we've been doing, right?

00:50:29.360 --> 00:50:32.130
But you didn't try to stop me just now.

00:50:32.130 --> 00:50:32.890
Why not?

00:50:36.810 --> 00:50:41.310
In reality, you want everyone to know your true self.

00:50:41.310 --> 00:50:43.730
You want them to discover your true self.

00:50:43.730 --> 00:50:47.570
You say nothing was left of Haruka Murakami after she adjusted herself to suit others?

00:50:47.900 --> 00:50:49.760
There's nothing that you want to do?

00:50:49.760 --> 00:50:51.010
That's a lie, I know it!

00:50:51.010 --> 00:50:52.050
Shut...

00:50:52.050 --> 00:50:54.290
I've seen just how selfish you can be.

00:50:54.900 --> 00:50:58.160
You wanted someone to find that part of you more than anything!

00:50:58.160 --> 00:50:58.910
Shut up!

00:51:00.540 --> 00:51:02.960
What could you possibly know about me?!

00:51:03.290 --> 00:51:04.400
Murakami...

00:51:04.400 --> 00:51:07.170
You don't know the first thing about me,
so don't assume you know how I feel.

00:51:07.750 --> 00:51:10.830
I mean, I don't even know how I feel myself.

00:51:18.140 --> 00:51:23.020
These clothes look great on someone as pretty as you, Haruka.

00:51:27.690 --> 00:51:29.450
Thank you, Auntie!

00:51:29.450 --> 00:51:32.490
I wish I could wear these every day!

00:51:36.220 --> 00:51:38.120
I don't know you fully either!

00:51:38.120 --> 00:51:42.570
But there's more to me than what was written on your flash cards.

00:51:42.570 --> 00:51:43.000
What?

00:51:43.310 --> 00:51:45.010
And that goes for you too!

00:51:45.010 --> 00:51:46.670
We both don't know much about each other,

00:51:46.670 --> 00:51:50.130
yet you turn a blind eye to yourself,
and reserve your criticism for others.

00:51:50.130 --> 00:51:50.880
Shut up!

00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:53.770
You were just afraid of being in the same world as others,

00:51:53.770 --> 00:51:55.760
so you ran away to your own little world!

00:51:55.760 --> 00:51:57.470
You're scared of getting hurt!

00:51:57.470 --> 00:51:58.470
So are you!

00:51:58.980 --> 00:52:01.140
You get hurt when someone touches a sore spot!

00:52:01.140 --> 00:52:01.900
Shut up!

00:52:01.900 --> 00:52:05.840
You think letting others decide your actions for you means you won't get hurt?

00:52:05.840 --> 00:52:08.090
But in reality you <i>are</i> choosing!

00:52:08.090 --> 00:52:08.640
You're wrong!

00:52:08.640 --> 00:52:10.410
Lifting your skirt in the hallway,

00:52:10.410 --> 00:52:11.890
or undressing at school...

00:52:11.890 --> 00:52:14.200
You mean you did all that because I wanted you to?

00:52:14.200 --> 00:52:18.000
That's a lie! You're just blaming me for what you wanted to do yourself!

00:52:18.000 --> 00:52:18.740
You're wrong!

00:52:18.740 --> 00:52:20.300
You're wrong, you're wrong!

00:52:20.300 --> 00:52:21.750
I...

00:52:26.250 --> 00:52:28.310
I don't stand out from the crowd.

00:52:28.310 --> 00:52:31.140
I perfect the personality desired of me.

00:52:31.140 --> 00:52:33.820
I'm a good girl who doesn't upset anyone.

00:52:33.820 --> 00:52:35.470
I was thinking the same thing!

00:52:35.990 --> 00:52:40.080
I have to be like that, or no one will love me.

00:52:51.990 --> 00:52:53.150
I love you.

00:53:13.920 --> 00:53:18.910
In return for not getting close to anyone,
I don't get on anyone's bad side.

00:53:18.910 --> 00:53:21.100
I shut myself away in my own little world,

00:53:21.100 --> 00:53:22.430
never actually trying.

00:53:23.160 --> 00:53:25.360
But you tried.

00:53:25.360 --> 00:53:28.360
You shift blame onto others, and you're selfish.

00:53:28.360 --> 00:53:29.690
But still,

00:53:29.690 --> 00:53:32.020
you try to be a good girl.

00:53:32.020 --> 00:53:35.740
You do your best to learn about those around you,

00:53:35.740 --> 00:53:39.210
and make friends without alienating anyone.

00:53:39.910 --> 00:53:43.320
You took that burden upon yourself,
without running away.

00:53:45.480 --> 00:53:47.620
I really respect you.

00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:50.710
I love you, Murakami.

00:53:52.450 --> 00:53:53.450
I see now.

00:53:56.130 --> 00:53:59.640
The reason I was able to enter your world

00:54:00.420 --> 00:54:03.740
was because I wanted to share that time with you.

00:54:05.810 --> 00:54:08.100
I'm the one who wanted it first.

00:54:10.310 --> 00:54:12.820
I like you too, Moritani.

00:54:14.500 --> 00:54:16.360
I...

00:54:17.300 --> 00:54:18.240
love you.

00:54:25.470 --> 00:54:27.200
<i>A few months passed,</i>

00:54:28.960 --> 00:54:32.920
<i>and I lost my ability to stop time.</i>

00:54:35.380 --> 00:54:37.470
<i>Even if I don't want to deal with something,</i>

00:54:38.010 --> 00:54:41.050
<i>I can no longer stop time and run away like before.</i>

00:54:41.530 --> 00:54:46.520
<i>I've started trying to be in the same world as others.</i>

00:54:47.940 --> 00:54:51.450
<i>I would be lying if I said it wasn't tough.</i>

00:54:51.450 --> 00:54:55.100
<i>I've become one person among many.</i>

00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:57.810
<i>I envy and get envied.</i>

00:54:57.810 --> 00:55:00.360
<i>I misunderstand,
get misunderstood, and upset others.</i>

00:55:01.250 --> 00:55:05.200
<i>And some don't even care about me at all.</i>

00:55:06.380 --> 00:55:09.680
<i>But even so, I still pull through.</i>

00:55:15.040 --> 00:55:17.510
<i>After all, this world</i>

00:55:20.810 --> 00:55:22.470
<i>has someone I love.</i>

00:59:49.350 --> 00:59:52.040
It was as a fleeting dream,

00:59:53.750 --> 00:59:55.220
but for the two of them,

00:59:56.150 --> 00:59:58.300
the time they shared was most definitely real.
